{"symbol":"CASP3","resolved":{"input":"CASP3","symbol":"CASP3","ncbi_gene_id":"836","name":"caspase 3","location":"4q35.1","aliases":["CPP32","CPP32B","SCA-1"],"uniprot":"P42574","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"CASP3 function (UniProt P42574, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Thiol protease that acts as a major effector caspase involved in the execution phase of apoptosis. Following cleavage and activation by initiator caspases (CASP8, CASP9 and/or CASP10), mediates execution of apoptosis by catalyzing cleavage of many proteins. At the onset of apoptosis, it proteolytically cleaves poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase PARP1 at a '216-Asp-|-Gly-217' bond. Cleaves and activates sterol regulatory element binding proteins (SREBPs) between the basic helix-loop-helix leucine zipper domain and the membrane attachment domain. Cleaves and activates caspase-6, -7 and -9 (CASP6, CASP7 and CASP9, respectively). Cleaves and inactivates interleukin-18 (IL18). Involved in the cleavage ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P42574","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P42574/entry","title":"CASP3: Caspase-3"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:10497198","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10497198/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:16374543","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16374543/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:17559062","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17559062/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:18723680","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18723680/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"CASP3 GO biological process annotations: apoptotic process, cellular response to staurosporine, erythrocyte differentiation, execution phase of apoptosis, intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway, negative regulation of cytokine production, neurotrophin TRK receptor signaling pathway, positive regulation of amyloid-beta formation, positive regulation of pyroptotic inflammatory response, protein c